# WN22-SO-000010: Windows Server 2022 must have the built-in guest account disabled.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-so-000010-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must have the built-in guest account disabled.`
    description `A system faces an increased vulnerability threat if the built-in guest account is not disabled. This is a known account that exists on all Windows systems and cannot be deleted. This account is initialized during the installation of the operating system with no password assigned.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,security-option,security-policy,ksi-iam-mfa`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-MFA,NIST-800-53:IA-8`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-MFA`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Accounts: Guest account status to "Disabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_MFA `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-MFA by enforcing EnableGuestAccount per the STIG (Built-in Guest account must be disabled (EnableGuestAccount = 0).). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_IA_8 `Windows Server implements IA-8 by enforcing EnableGuestAccount per the STIG (Built-in Guest account must be disabled (EnableGuestAccount = 0).). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `EnableGuestAccount`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 0
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
